# No third-party media-player style

Committed files must not use another media player as a design shorthand. Explain the behavior;
do not say a design is "in the style of", "like", or "similar to" another product.

## Don't

- `<product>-style` handoff, player chrome, or queue behavior
- `like <product>` or `similar to <product>` as a design label
- Any other comparison that names another media player to stand in for a design

## Do

Name the behavior in Podverse terms:

- Exclusive active-device handoff (opening device 2 pauses device 1)
- A first-class media-app contract (background audio and car menus from a long-lived native
  service)

## Still fine

Protocol and platform names that are the actual subject — RSS `itunes:*` tags, CarPlay, Android
Auto, Apple as a platform vendor — are not style comparisons. Generated or ingested feed text that
happens to mention another app is also out of scope.

